            "grounded_block": "NEX Indonesia knowledge (grounded · cite the region/topic when useful, do not embellish):\n  · [tourism.jakarta · DKI Jakarta · stable · verified 2026-08-30T00:00:00.000Z]\n    Jakarta is Indonesia's capital and largest city — a business hub rather than a classic tourist destination. Highlights: Kota Tua (old Dutch quarter with cafés and museums), Monas (National Monument), Istiqlal Mosque (South-East Asia's largest, next door to the Catholic cathedral), Taman Mini Indonesia Indah (culture park), night markets in Glodok (Chinatown), and Pantai Indah Kapuk for modern food streets. Traffic is heavy — plan indoor blocks and use Gojek/Grab or MRT/TransJakarta buses.\n  · [indonesia.capital · Indonesia · stable · verified 2026-08-30T00:00:00.000Z]\n    The capital of Indonesia is Jakarta, on the north-west coast of Java. Since 2019 the government has been progressively moving parts of the administrative capital to Nusantara (IKN) in East Kalimantan; Jakarta remains the largest city and economic centre.\n  · [accommodation.regional.jakarta_business · DKI Jakarta · stable · verified 2026-08-30T16:05:43.447Z]\n    Jakarta's business-hotel inventory concentrates in the SCBD, Sudirman, Thamrin, and Kuningan corridors, with international chains including Ritz-Carlton, Grand Hyatt, Fairmont, Mandarin Oriental, and Four Seasons. Mid-market properties spread through South Jakarta (Kemang, Blok M). Airport hotels cluster at Soekarno-Hatta."
