            "grounded_block": "NEX Indonesia knowledge (grounded · cite the region/topic when useful, do not embellish):\n  · [food.nasi_goreng · Indonesia · stable · verified 2026-08-30T00:00:00.000Z]\n    Nasi goreng is Indonesian fried rice — rice stir-fried with kecap manis (sweet soy sauce), garlic, shallots, chilli and often chicken, egg or prawn. Usually served with a fried egg on top, prawn crackers and slices of cucumber and tomato. Considered the national dish and available almost everywhere from street stalls to hotels.\n  · [food.rendang · West Sumatra · stable · verified 2026-08-30T00:00:00.000Z]\n    Rendang is a slow-cooked beef curry from West Sumatra (Padang cuisine). Beef is simmered for hours in coconut milk with lemongrass, galangal, turmeric, kaffir lime and chilli until the liquid reduces and the meat turns dark and rich. Best found at Padang restaurants (rumah makan Padang) — the classic ordering style is a bench of small dishes brought to your table, you pay for what you eat.\n  · [food.sate · Indonesia · stable · verified 2026-08-30T00:00:00.000Z]\n    Sate (satay) is skewered grilled meat served with a dipping sauce. Common types: sate ayam (chicken, sweet peanut sauce), sate kambing (goat), sate lilit (Balinese minced fish/meat wrapped on lemongrass stems). Look for sate stalls with lit charcoal in the evening — that's when they're at their best."
          }
